<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Four estates (Sasanian)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The four estates were the social classes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>: priests, warriors, scribes and commoners such as peasants and artisans. This hierarchy, supported by Zoroastrian teaching, defined social status and duties and was a key part of Sasanian ideology.</p></div>
